          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ♭
                  %mo →
                  %mi Π
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\flat \to \Pi
          %p
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+modality"} flat modality
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shape+modality"} shape modality
            may be thought of as sending “points to the pieces in which they sit”.
          %h2#definition_and_basic_properties Definition and basic properties
          %p
            Notice the existence of the following canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformations"} natural transformations
            induced from the structure of a cohesive topos (a special case of the construction at
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unity+of+opposites"} unity of opposites
          #TransformationFromPointsToPieces.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+topos"} cohesive topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              with (
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ʃ
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mo ♭
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} &amp;#643; \dashv \flat
              ) its (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shape+modality"} shape modality
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊣
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \dashv
              = succeed ")-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+modality"} flat modality
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ♭
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi ʃ
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\flat X \longrightarrow X \longrightarrow &amp;#643; X
            %p
              (given by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
              of the
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ♭
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \flat
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/counit+of+a+comonad"} counit
              followed by the
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ʃ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} &amp;#643;
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+a+monad"} unit
              %strong from points to their pieces
              or the
              = succeed "," do
                %strong points-to-pieces-transformation
            %p
              If this is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
              for all
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %em pieces have points
              or that the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nullstellensatz"} Nullstellensatz
              is verified.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              The
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %mo ⊣
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f^\ast \dashv f_\ast)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunct"} adjunct
              of the transformation from pieces to points, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TransformationFromPointsToPieces"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ♭
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi ʃ
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\flat X \longrightarrow X \longrightarrow &amp;#643; X
            %p
              is (by the rule of forming right
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjuncts"} adjuncts
              by first applying the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
              functor and then precomposing with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+an+adjunction"} unit
              and by the fact that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunct"} adjunct
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+an+adjunction"} unit
              is the
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity"} identity
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo !
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %mi X
                      %mo ⟶
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mo !
                      %mi X
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mo ≃
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mo !
                      %mi X
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (f_\ast X \longrightarrow f_! X)
                    \\coloneqq
                    \\left(
                    f_\ast X \longrightarrow f_\ast f^\ast f_! X \stackrel{\simeq}{\longrightarrow} f_!X
                    \\right)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Observe that going backwards by applying
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\ast
              to this and postcomposing with the
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %mo ⊣
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f^\ast \dashv f_\ast)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/counit+of+an+adjunction"} counit
              is equivalent to just applying
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\ast
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+monad"} idempotency
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ♭
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \flat
              the counit is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+object"} discrete object
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mo !
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\ast f_! X
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mo ♭
                      %mi X
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi X
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi ʃ
                      %mi X
                      %mo )
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %mi X
                      %mo ⟶
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mo !
                      %mi X
                      %mo )
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left(
                    \\flat X \longrightarrow X \longrightarrow &amp;#643; X
                    \\right)
                    \=
                    f^\ast \left(
                    f_\ast X \longrightarrow f_! X
                    \\right).
            %p
              Observe then finally that since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\ast
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
              precisely if its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunct"} adjunct
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo !
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_\ast X \longrightarrow f_! X
              is, respectively.
            %p If this adjunct
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ♭
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ϵ
                          %mo ♭
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi η
                          %mo ♯
                    %mo ♯
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\flat X
                    \\overset{\epsilon^{\flat}}{\longrightarrow}
                    X
                    \\overset{\eta^\sharp}{\longrightarrow}
                    \\sharp X
            %p
              is a monomorphism, we say that
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+objects"} discrete objects
                  are
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+objects"} concrete
          %h2#relation_to_points_to_copieces Relation to points to co-pieces
          #PiecesHavePointsIfDiscreteObjectsAreConcrete.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pieces+have+points"} pieces have points
                iff
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+objects+are+concrete"} discrete objects are concrete
            %p
              For a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+topos"} cohesive topos
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %em> pieces have points
                  , i.e.
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ♭
                        %mi X
                        %mo →
                        %mi X
                        %mo →
                        %mi ʃ
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \flat X \to X \to &amp;#643; X
                  is an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
                  for all
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                          %mo ∈
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi H
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in \mathbf{H}
              %li
                %p
                  %em>
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+objects"} discrete objects
                    are
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+objects"} concrete
                  , i.e.
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ♭
                        %mi X
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mrow
                            %msubsup
                              %mi η
                              %mrow
                                %mo ♭
                                %mi X
                              %mo ♯
                        %mo ♯
                        %mo ♭
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \flat X \overset{ \eta^{\sharp}_{\flat X} }{\longrightarrow} \sharp \flat X
                  is a
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
          %p
            See at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+topos"} cohesive topos
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "cohesive+topos#PiecesHavePointsEquivalentToDiscreteObjectsAreConcrete"} this prop.
          %h2#RelationToAufhebung Relation to Aufhebung of the initial opposition
          %p
            For a cohesive 1-topos, if the pieces-to-points transform is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
            then there is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Aufhebung"} Aufhebung
            of the initial opposition
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ∅
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\emptyset \dashv \ast)
            in that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ♯
                  %mi ∅
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi ∅
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sharp \emptyset \simeq \emptyset
            (
            %a{:href => "#LawvereMenni15"}> Lawvere-Menni 15, lemma 4.1
            , see also
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Shulman15"} Shulman 15, section 3
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+topos"} base topos
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boolean+topos"} Boolean topos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
            (
            %a{:href => "#LawvereMenni15"}> Lawvere-Menni 15, lemma 4.2
            ).
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#BundleEquivalenceAndConcordance Bundle equivalence and concordance
          %p
            Given an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group"} ∞-group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}(X,\mathbf{B}G)
            is that of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+%E2%88%9E-bundles"} principal ∞-bundles
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalences"} equivalences
            between them. Alternatively one may form the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [X,\mathbf{B}G]
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shape+modality"} shape modality
            to this yields the
            = succeed "-groupoid" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi ʃ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}^\infty(X,\mathbf{B}G) \coloneqq  &amp;#643; [X,\mathbf{B}G]
            of
            = succeed "-principal" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "-bundles" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concordances"} concordances
            between them. Alternatively, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+modality"} flat modality
            applied to the internal hom is again just the external hom
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ♭
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ≃
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \flat [X,\mathbf{B}G] \simeq \mathbf{H}(X,\mathbf{B}G)
          %p In conclusion, in this situation the points-to-pieces transform is the canonical map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{H}(X,\mathbf{B}G) \longrightarrow \mathbf{H}^\infty(X,\mathbf{B}G)
          %p
            from
            = succeed "-principal" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "-bundles" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "-principal" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "-bundles" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %h3#InGlobalEquivariantHomotopyTheory In global equivariant homotopy theory
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+equivariant+homotopy+theory"} global equivariant homotopy theory
            an incarnation of the points to pieces transform is the comparison map from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+quotients"} homotopy quotients
            to ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotients"} quotients
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi G
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  X//G \longrightarrow X/G
          %p
            which in terms of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Borel+construction"} Borel construction
            is induced by the map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E G \to \ast
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mi G
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mi G
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mi G
                  %mi X
                  %mo =
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi G
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  E G \times_G X \longrightarrow \ast \times_G X = X/G
                  \\,.
          %p
            (see at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+equivariant+homotopy+theory"} global equivariant homotopy theory
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "global+equivariant+homotopy+theory#OrdinaryQuotientAndHomotopyQuotientViaCohesion"} this prop.
          %h3#in_tangent_cohesion_the_differential_cohomology_diagram In tangent cohesion: the differential cohomology diagram
          %p
            In a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} tangent cohesive (∞,1)-topos
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+types"} stable homotopy types
            the points-to-pieces transform is one stage in a natural hexagonal
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/long+exact+sequence"} long exact sequence
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology+diagram"} differential cohomology diagram
          %h3#comparison_map_between_algebraic_and_topological_ktheory Comparison map between algebraic and topological K-theory
          %p
            Applied to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+types"} stable homotopy types
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Stab
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi T
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Stab(\mathbf{H}) \hookrightarrow T\mathbf{H}
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} tangent cohesive (∞,1)-topos
            which arise from a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} symmetric monoidal (∞,1)-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi CMon
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Cat
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \in CMon_\infty(Cat_\infty(\mathbf{H}))
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} internal
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            under internal
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+K-theory+of+a+symmetric+monoidal+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} algebraic K-theory of a symmetric monoidal (∞,1)-category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comparison+map+between+algebraic+and+topological+K-theory"} comparison map between algebraic and topological K-theory
          %h3#in_infinitesimal_cohesion In infinitesimal cohesion
          %p
